You can override table names in config/userlogs.php

//IF LOGGING IN FROM A USER WITH PERMISSIONS TO LOGIN TO ANY ACCOUNT
//THIS IS THE Session::get('variable') THAT WILL GET THE ORIGINAL USER
'orig_user' => 'currentUserId',

in your config/app.php providers array:
Exults\Logs\LogsServiceProvider::class,

in aliases array:
'UserLogs'  => Exults\Logs\LogsServiceProvider::class,

in autoload psr-4 in composer.json:
"Exults\\Logs\\": "packages/exults/logs/src/"

put in BeforeMiddleware:
UserLogs::log();

To log the time each request takes, put this in your middleware:
    public function terminate()
    {
        UserLog::logEnd();
    }




